# 🚀 Getting Started

## 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```
git clone https://github.com/your-username/ayurvision-ai.git
cd ayurvision-ai
```

---

# ⚙️ Backend Setup

### Requirements

* Node.js (LTS)
* MongoDB

Create `.env` inside `backend/`

```
MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/ayurvision_ai
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key
PORT=3001
AI_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

Install dependencies:

```
cd backend
npm install
```

Run backend:

```
npm run dev
```

Backend runs at:

```
http://localhost:3001
```

---

# 🤖 AI Service Setup

Navigate to AI service:

```
cd ai-service
```

Create virtual environment:

```
python -m venv venv
```

Activate environment

Windows:

```
venv\Scripts\activate
```

Mac/Linux:

```
source venv/bin/activate
```

Install dependencies:

```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Dataset Structure

Place dataset inside:

```
datasets/
   Indian Medicinal Leaves Image Dataset/
      Medicinal plant dataset/
         Neem/
         Tulsi/
         Brahmi/
```

Each folder represents a **class label**.

---

## Train the Model

```
python train.py
```

After training:

* Model saved in `ai-service/model/`
* Class labels saved in `class_names.txt`

---

## Run AI API

```
python api.py
```

AI service runs at:

```
http://localhost:5000
```

---

# 💻 Frontend Setup

Install dependencies:

```
cd frontend
npm install
```

Run development server:

```
npm run dev
```

Frontend runs at:

```
http://localhost:5173
```

---

# 🔌 API Endpoints

## Authentication

```
POST /api/auth/signup
POST /api/auth/login
```

---

## Image Upload

```
POST /api/upload
```

Headers:

```
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

Form Data:

```
image: <file>
```

Uploaded images can be accessed at:

```
GET /uploads/<filename>
```

